<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman ups Accor target.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman ups Accor target.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said on Thursday it raised its 12-month price target for French hotels group Accor to 1,050 francs from 890 francs.</p>
<p>In a research note, analyst Fraser Ramzan at the investment bank also said he repeated an &quot;outperform&quot; rating on the stock.</p>
<p>He said Accor had greater scope for recovery in its operating results due to its heavy exposure to upmarket and mid-market hotels in France and Germany.</p>
<p>The stock was up 1.1 percent at 935 francs.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
